cord infection and puerperal sepsis among neonates and their mothers in rural Mwanza Region, Tanzania", "abstract": "A  
study was carried out in Misungwi and Kwimba Districts, Tanzania to determine the effectiveness of clean delivery kits  
in preventing cord infection and puerperal sepsis... randomised stepped-wedge design schedule..."},                     
    {"study_index": 22, "title": "Community perspective of maternal mortality: experience from Konduga local government 
area, Borno State, Nigeria", "abstract": "BACKGROUND/OBJECTIVE High maternal mortality in Nigeria... METHOD The study   
took place between 10th October and 10th December 2003. An in-depth interview guide..."},                               
    {"study_index": 23, "title": "Does improving maternal knowledge of vaccines impact infant immunization rates? A     
community-based randomized-controlled trial in Karachi, Pakistan", "abstract": "BACKGROUND In Pakistan, only 59-73% of  
children 12-23 months of age are fully immunized. This randomized, controlled trial was conducted to assess the impact  
of a low-literacy immunization promotion educational intervention..."},                                                 
    {"study_index": 24, "title": "Global, regional, and national causes of child mortality in 2008: a systematic        
analysis", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Up-to-date information on the causes of child deaths is crucial to guide global      
efforts to improve child survival. We report new estimates for 2008..."},                                               
    {"study_index": 25, "title": "PRISM (program of resources, information and support for mothers): a                  
community-randomised trial to reduce depression and improve women's physical health six months after birth", "abstract":
"BACKGROUND In the year after birth one in six women has a depressive illness... cluster-randomised trial involving 16  
rural and metropolitan communities..."},                                                                                
    {"study_index": 26, "title": "Impact of traditional birth attendant training in Mozambique: a controlled study",    
"abstract": "This study was designed to assess the utility and impact on perinatal mortality of a model traditional     
birth attendant (TBA) training program in rural Mozambique..."},                                                        
    {"study_index": 27, "title": "WHO systematic review of maternal morbidity and mortality: the prevalence of severe   
acute maternal morbidity (near miss)", "abstract": "AIM: To determine the prevalence of severe acute maternal morbidity 
(SAMM) worldwide (near miss). METHOD: Systematic review of all available data..."},                                     
    {"study_index": 28, "title": "Maternal health in poor countries: the broader context and a call for action",        
"abstract": "In this paper, we take a broad perspective on maternal health and place it in its wider context..."},      
    {"study_index": 29, "title": "Effect of home-based neonatal care and management of sepsis on neonatal mortality:    
field trial in rural India", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Neonatal care is not available to most neonates in developing      
countries... We chose 39 intervention and 47 control villages in the Gadchiroli district in India..."},                 
    {"study_index": 30, "title": "Alleviating perinatal depressive symptoms and stress: a nurse-community health worker 
randomized trial", "abstract": "To determine whether a Nurse-Community Health Worker (CHW) home visiting team... would  
demonstrate greater reduction of depressive symptoms and stress..."},                                                   
    {"study_index": 31, "title": "Maternal mortality: who, when, where, and why", "abstract": "The risk of a woman dying
as a result of pregnancy or childbirth during her lifetime is about one in six in the poorest parts of the world..."},  
    {"study_index": 32, "title": "Decline in maternal mortality in Matlab, Bangladesh: a cautionary tale", "abstract":  
"BACKGROUND A study in Matlab, Bangladesh, has provided evidence favouring a community-based maternity-care delivery    
system... Caution is required in the interpretation of short-term trends in one indicator in studies designed without   
random allocation..."},                                                                                                 
    {"study_index": 33, "title": "NGO facilitation of a government community-based maternal and neonatal health         
programme in rural India: improvements in equity", "abstract": "Socio-economic disparities in health have been well     
documented around the world. This study examines whether NGO facilitation of the government's community-based health    
programme improved the equity of maternal and newborn health... A quasi-experimental study design..."},                 
    {"study_index": 34, "title": "Impact of reduced maternal exposures to wood smoke from an introduced chimney stove on
newborn birth weight in rural Guatemala", "abstract": "BACKGROUND A growing body of evidence indicates a relationship   
between household indoor air pollution from cooking fires and adverse neonatal outcomes, such as low birth weight       
(LBW)... RESPIRE (Randomized Exposure Study of Pollution Indoors and Respiratory Effects)..."},                         
    {"study_index": 35, "title": "Statistical methods for examining heterogeneity and combining results from several    
studies in meta-analysis", "abstract": "This chapter contains section titled: Summary Points Meta—Analysis Formulae for 
Estimates of Effect from Individual Studies..."},                                                                       
    {"study_index": 36, "title": "Women's groups practising participatory learning and action to improve maternal and   
newborn health in low-resource settings: a systematic review and meta-analysis", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Maternal and   
neonatal mortality rates remain high in many low-income and middle-income countries... We did a systematic review and   
meta-analysis of randomised controlled trials..."},                                                                     
    {"study_index": 37, "title": "Implementing community-based perinatal care: results from a pilot study in rural      
Pakistan", "abstract": "OBJECTIVE This pilot study investigated the feasibility of delivering a package of              
community-based interventions for improving perinatal care using lady health workers (LHWs) and traditional birth       
attendants (Dais) in rural Pakistan... four of eight village clusters..."},                                             
    {"study_index": 38, "title": "An intervention to improve postpartum outcomes in African-American mothers: a         
randomised controlled trial", "abstract": "OBJECTIVE:To evaluate the efficacy of an integrated multiple risk            
intervention, delivered mainly during pregnancy, in reducing such risks (cigarette smoking, environmental tobacco smoke 
exposure, depression, and intimate partner violence) postpartum... Clinic-based, individually tailored counseling..."}, 
    {"study_index": 39, "title": "The Tanzania Connect Project: a cluster-randomized trial of the child survival impact 
of adding paid community health workers to an existing facility-focused health system", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Tanzania
has been a pioneer in establishing community-level services... The Tanzania Connect Project is a randomized cluster     
trial located in three rural districts..."},                                                                            
    {"study_index": 40, "title": "Improvement of perinatal and newborn care in rural Pakistan through community-based   
strategies: a cluster-randomised effectiveness trial", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Newborn deaths account for 57% of deaths 
in children younger than 5 years in Pakistan... We aimed to evaluate the effectiveness of a community-based intervention
package... cluster randomised trial..."}                                                                                
]                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                        
# Selection criteria from protocol:                                                                                     
# - All prospective randomised, cluster-randomised and quasi-randomised trials                                          
# - Evaluating effectiveness of community-based intervention packages                                                   
# - In reducing maternal and neonatal mortality and morbidities                                                         
# - And improving neonatal outcomes                                                                                     
                                                                                                                        
decisions = []                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
for study in studies:                                                                                                   
    idx = study['study_index']                                                                                          
    title = study['title']                                                                                              
    abstract = study['abstract'].lower()                                                                                
                                                                                                                        
    decision = None                                                                                                     
    rationale = ""                                                                                                      
    confidence = "high"                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                        
    # Check for trial design keywords                                                                                   
    is_trial = any(keyword in abstract for keyword in ['randomised', 'randomized', 'cluster-randomised',                
'cluster-randomized', 'stepped-wedge', 'quasi-experimental', 'field trial'])                                            
                                                                                                                        
    # Check for community-based intervention                                                                            
    is_community_based = any(keyword in abstract for keyword in ['community', 'village', 'home-based', 'lady health     
worker', 'traditional birth attendant', 'health worker'])                                                               
                                                                                                                        
    # Check for relevant outcomes                                                                                       
    has_maternal_outcome = any(keyword in abstract for keyword in ['maternal mortality', 'puerperal sepsis',            
'obstetric', 'postpartum'])                                                                                             
    has_neonatal_outcome = any(keyword in abstract for keyword in ['neonatal mortality', 'cord infection', 'perinatal', 
'stillbirth', 'birth weight', 'low birth weight', 'infant mortality'])                                                  
                                                                                                                        
    # Specific exclusions                                                                                               
    is_review = any(keyword in abstract for keyword in ['systematic review', 'meta-analysis', 'review of', 'statistical 
methods'])                                                                                                              
    is_qualitative = any(keyword in abstract for keyword in ['qualitative', 'in-depth interview', 'perspective', 'call  
for action'])                                                                                                           
    is_opinion = any(keyword in abstract for keyword in ['opinion', 'editorial', 'commentary', 'broader context'])      
                                                                                                                        
    # Decision logic                                                                                                    
    if is_review or is_qualitative or is_opinion:                                                                       
        decision = "EXCLUDE"                                                                                            
        if is_review:                                                                                                   
            rationale = f"This is a {title.split(':')[-1].strip() if ':' in title else 'review/meta-analysis'}, not a   
primary trial. Does not meet study design criteria."                                                                    
        elif is_qualitative:                                                                                            
            rationale = f"This is a qualitative study using interviews/surveys, not a                                   
randomised/cluster-randomised/quasi-randomised trial."                                                                  
        else:                                                                                                           
            rationale = f"This is an opinion/policy paper, not a primary trial."                                        
    elif not is_trial:                                                                                                  
        decision = "EXCLUDE"                                                                                            
        rationale = f"This study does not appear to be a randomised, cluster-randomised, or quasi-randomised trial.     
Study design unclear or observational."                                                                                 
    elif not is_community_based:                                                                                        
        decision = "EXCLUDE"                                                                                            
        rationale = f"This study does not appear to evaluate a community-based intervention package."                   
    elif not (has_maternal_outcome or has_neonatal_outcome):                                                            
        decision = "EXCLUDE"                                                                                            
        rationale = f"This study does not evaluate maternal/neonatal mortality, morbidity, or neonatal outcomes. Focuses
on other outcomes."                                                                                                     
    else:                                                                                                               
        decision = "INCLUDE"                                                                                            
        if 'randomised' in abstract or 'randomized' in abstract:                                                        
            design_type = "randomised/cluster-randomised trial"                                                         
        elif 'quasi' in abstract or 'field trial' in abstract:                                                          
            design_type = "quasi-randomised/field trial"                                                                
        else:                                                                                                           
            design_type = "trial"                                                                                       
        rationale = f"This is a {design_type} evaluating a community-based intervention package. Outcomes include       
relevant maternal/neonatal outcomes. Meets all selection criteria."                                                     
                                                                                                                        
    decisions.append({                                                                                                  
        "study_index": idx,                                                                                             
        "title": title,                                                                                                 
        "decision": decision,                                                                                           
        "rationale": rationale,                                                                                         
        "confidence": confidence                                                                                        
    })                                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                        
# Count totals                                                                                                          
n_included = sum(1 for d in decisions if d['decision'] == 'INCLUDE')                                                    
n_excluded = sum(1 for d in decisions if d['decision'] == 'EXCLUDE')                                                    
                                                                                                                        
result = {                                                                                                              
    "n_total": len(decisions),                                                                                          
    "n_included": n_included,                                                                                           
    "n_excluded": n_excluded,                                                                                           
    "decisions": decisions                                                                                              
}                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                        
print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))                                                                                     
                                                                                                                        
