to promote birth and newborn care preparedness; made four postnatal home visits to negotiate preventive care practices  
and to assess newborns for illness; and referred sick neonates to a hospital and facilitated compliance. Primary outcome
measures were antenatal and immediate newborn care behaviours, knowledge of danger signs, care seeking for neonatal     
complications, and neonatal mortality. FINDINGS A total of 4616 and 5241 live births were recorded from 9987 and 11153  
